      "author": {
        "id": "0194f481-44a0-7f90-ab3d-189d8506bb3a",
        "username": "ferris",
        "display_name": "Ferris"
      },
      "content": "I get error E0502 when I push to a vector while holding a reference to its first element:\n\n```rust\nlet mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];\nlet first = &v[0];\nv.push(4);\nprintln!(\"{first}\");\n```\n\nWhy is this a problem if I only read `first`?",
      "created_at": "2026-10-10T14:02:00Z",
      "edited_at": null,
      "is_solution": false
    },
    {
      "id": "01a12666-4900-7d32-b9e0-d1b391585d16",
      "number": 2,
      "parent_id": null,
      "author": {
        "id": "019505c2-b000-7fa1-8db2-667fbae6e2ce",
        "username": "corro",
        "display_name": "Corro the Unsafe"
      },
      "content": "`push` may reallocate the buffer, so `first` could point at freed memory. The borrow checker cannot know the capacity, so it rejects every `&mut` borrow while a shared borrow is alive.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-10T15:20:00Z",
      "edited_at": null,
      "is_solution": false
    },
